  "Question": "Let \\(f(x)=ax^7+bx^3+cx-5,\\) where \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) and \\(c\\) are constants. If \\(f(-7)=7,\\) then \\(f(7)\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-17\\)",
    "B": "\\(-7\\)",
    "C": "\\(14\\)",
    "D": "\\(21\\)",
    "E": "not uniquely determined"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "All the nonconstant powers are odd. Replacing \\(x\\) by \\(-x\\) therefore reverses the sign of every nonconstant term, while the constant remains \\(-5\\). Adding the two expressions cancels all terms containing the unknown coefficients:\n\\[\nf(x)+f(-x)=-5-5=-10.\n\\]\nTaking \\(x=7\\) and using \\(f(-7)=7\\), we obtain\n\\[\nf(7)=-10-f(-7)=-10-7=\\boxed{-17}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
